status.description:
Whether saving the policy rule succeeded or failed; present only when
`kind` is `policyPersistence`. A failure does not undo the decision;
only the saved rule is missing.

windowTitle.description:
The target window's title: the app's own text, which a page can set;
a client shows it quoted and as plain text, never as markup or a
choice, and may cap it.

optOutNotificationMethods.description:
Exact notification method names the client declines; no wildcards;
unknown names accepted and ignored; the protected set (SS1.7) cannot
be opted out.

readableAfterAt.description:
RFC3339 `recordedAt` of the first readable record after the range;
always present, since a range is read past only when readable
records follow it (ADR 60914 D1).

oneOf.description:
Admission id is unknown (`-32070`, amendment 45445 FR-45445-13);
`data.sessionId` and `data.admissionId` name the rejected pair.
Experimental tier (owner ruling on PR #50979 carries the plane).

maxLimits.description:
The host's posture ceiling as a five-axis limits object (tdd SS1.10;
ADR 39851-ss1-10 D1; ADR 59770 D4): what a connection may choose.
**Experimental, same-user socket only** (`InitializeResult.maxLimits`;
stripped for unopted callers per SS1.5.1); absent means the host has
no limits regime, so there is nothing to narrow and no read method
to serve. Absent is never fabricated.

deliveryNumber.description:
`scheduledFire`: the occurrence number within the job's
history, present with occurrence metadata (tdd SS4.5.17;
ADR 45446 D2).

emittedAtMs.description:
Emission time in Unix milliseconds, recorded once at emission;
server→client notifications only (SS1.2.5). Optional on the wire so
decoders tolerate older servers.

windowTokens.description:
The effective context-window size from the host's pressure basis;
absent when the basis has no limit — the limit part is omitted,
never invented (tdd SS4.6.6).

tierName.description:
The subscription tier's display name from the refresh mint, when it
returned one. Clients print this, never `usage.tier` (the tier id;
spec 18742 US-FR-003).
